==English==

===Etymology===
From the act of tying or even nailing a pigeon to a stool to act as a decoy for hunters.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-au-stool pigeon.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A decoy or an [[informer]], especially one who is a [[spy]] for the police.
#: {{syn|en|stoolie|stooly|Thesaurus:informant}}

